{"type": "agent", "t": 1793457100.0720828, "agent": "E:s1_param_sweep", "role": "E", "parent": "P", "model": "zai/glm-5.3", "label": "Find the exact FILTER carrier param that makes the descrambled speech maximally ", "id": "h4"}
{"type": "dag", "t": 1793457100.0720828, "op": "add", "node": "s1_param_sweep", "by": "P", "objective": "Find the exact FILTER carrier param that makes the descrambled speech maximally intelligible, and extract the full spoken text (possible flag) via ASR, persisting all transcripts to work/.", "deps": [], "assignee": "E:s1_param_sweep", "detail": "Continue from work/NOTES.md (read it first). Facts: kernel kD (DEMOD freq_off=25000, FILTER param=3600 via xor chain at instr 18-25, instr 26 nop'd) produced work/outD.wav, which ASR (faster-whisper small) transcribed as: 'Рефивер сервис мессендж... Тюнинг на шум... В конце сервиса мессендж' — a service message, no flag yet. Task: 1) Re-run ASR on outD.wav with model medium, language ru AND en, beam_size 5, persist full transcripts to work/transcript_D_medium_ru.txt / _en.txt. 2) Sweep FILTER param: build kernel variants from kD (work/kernel_off25k_prm3600.kdsp) by patching instruction 26 (movi r8, imm) to imm values {2800, 3000, 3200, 3300, 3500, 3600, 3700, 4000} (keep instruction 16 = 25000); run files/dsp_vm files/capture.iq <variant> work/out_p<param>.wav; run whisper small ru on each; persist everything to work/sweep_asr.txt. 3) Also listen-proxy: compute a simple intelligibility metric (e.g. spectral flatness in 300-3400 Hz band) per param. 4) Report the best transcript verbatim and whether any ctfcup{...} appears. Keep every intermediate file in work/. python is available on Windows; asr2.py in work/ shows the working faster-whisper invocation pattern.", "id": "h5"}
{"type": "agent", "t": 1793457100.072211, "agent": "E:s2_rf_tune", "role": "E", "parent": "P", "model": "zai/glm-5.3", "label": "Analyze the full 240 kHz RF spectrum of capture.iq for OTHER signals besides the", "id": "h6"}
{"type": "dag", "t": 1793457100.072211, "op": "add", "node": "s2_rf_tune", "by": "P", "objective": "Analyze the full 240 kHz RF spectrum of capture.iq for OTHER signals besides the 25 kHz one (per the spoken hint 'Тюнинг на шум'), demodulate candidates offline, and ASR them for the flag.", "deps": [], "assignee": "E:s2_rf_tune", "detail": "Continue from work/NOTES.md (read it first). Facts: files/capture.iq = 3,057,880 complex float32 samples at 240 kS/s (12.74 s). Demodulating at freq_off=+25000 Hz (kernel kD) yields a 48 kHz audio containing a scrambled-then-descrambled 'service message' that ends with 'Тюнинг на шум' (tune to the noise) — no flag found in it. The hint 'tune the noise' suggests the REAL payload may be at a different center frequency in the wideband capture, possibly hidden near/below the noise floor. Task: 1) Compute the full averaged power spectrum of capture.iq (Welch, fine resolution); plot to work/rf_spectrum.png and list ALL noticeable energy concentrations (center, bandwidth, level) — not just the obvious 25 kHz one. 2) For each candidate center (including weak ones near noise floor, and image/negative frequencies), implement the same DEMOD chain offline in numpy (DDC with -2*pi*off/240000 phase, 163-tap Kaiser beta=6.5 cutoff 13.5 kHz decimate-by-5, FM discriminator atan2 consecutive products * 1.527887453682195, DC removal, 300-3400 bandpass — see NOTES.md section 5), save work/tune_<off>.wav. 3) Run faster-whisper small (ru and en) on each candidate audio; persist to work/tune_asr.txt. 4) Report whether any candidate yields speech containing ctfcup{...} or intelligible Russian. Persist a summary to work/rf_recon.md. audio_demod25k.npy (float demod at 25 kHz) already exists if useful.", "id": "h7"}
